<a name="soporte"></a>🔧 CONCEPTOS DE SOPORTE TÉCNICO
Health Check (Verificación de Salud)
Qué es: Verificar que un endpoint/servicio esté funcionando correctamente.
Niveles de Health Check:
1. Básico (Ping)
java// Solo verifica si responde
public HealthCheckResponse simpleCheck(String url) {
    try {
        HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) new URL(url).openConnection();
        conn.setRequestMethod("GET");
        conn.setConnectTimeout(5000);
        
        int statusCode = conn.getResponseCode();
        
        return HealthCheckResponse.builder()
            .status(statusCode == 200 ? "UP" : "DOWN")
            .statusCode(statusCode)
            .build();
    } catch (Exception e) {
        return HealthCheckResponse.builder()
            .status("DOWN")
            .message(e.getMessage())
            .build();
    }
}
2. Intermedio (Con Métricas)
javapublic HealthCheckResponse intermediateCheck(String url) {
    long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
    
    try {
        HttpURLConnection conn = (HttpURLConnection) new URL(url).openConnection();
        conn.setRequestMethod("GET");
        
        int statusCode = conn.getResponseCode();
        long responseTime = System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime;
        
        // Analizar respuesta
        String status = determineStatus(statusCode, responseTime);
        List<String> issues = detectIssues(statusCode, responseTime);
        
        return HealthCheckResponse.builder()
            .status(status)
            .statusCode(statusCode)
            .responseTimeMs(responseTime)
            .issues(issues)
            .build();
    } catch (Exception e) {
        return buildErrorResponse(e);
    }
}

private String determineStatus(int code, long latency) {
    if (code >= 200 && code < 300) {
        return latency > 3000 ? "DEGRADED" : "UP";
    }
    return "DOWN";
}
3. Avanzado (Diagnóstico Completo)
javapublic DiagnosticReport fullDiagnosis(DiagnosticRequest request) {
    DiagnosticReport report = DiagnosticReport.builder()
        .diagnosticId(UUID.randomUUID().toString())
        .timestamp(LocalDateTime.now())
        .build();
    
    // 1. Validar autenticación
    AuthenticationAnalysis authAnalysis = analyzeAuth(request);
    report.setAuthAnalysis(authAnalysis);
    
    // 2. Validar payload
    if (request.getRequestBody() != null) {
        PayloadAnalysis payloadAnalysis = analyzePayload(request.getRequestBody());
        report.setPayloadAnalysis(payloadAnalysis);
    }
    
    // 3. Ejecutar request y analizar respuesta
    ResponseAnalysis responseAnalysis = executeAndAnalyze(request);
    report.setResponseAnalysis(responseAnalysis);
    
    // 4. Medir performance
    PerformanceAnalysis perfAnalysis = analyzePerformance(request);
    report.setPerformanceAnalysis(perfAnalysis);
    
    // 5. Generar recomendaciones
    generateRecommendations(report);
    
    return report;
}
```

**Qué se mide en un Health Check:**
- ✅ **Disponibilidad** - ¿Responde?
- ⏱️ **Latencia** - ¿Qué tan rápido?
- 📊 **Status Code** - ¿200, 500, 404?
- 🔒 **SSL/TLS** - ¿Certificado válido?
- 📦 **Content Type** - ¿JSON, XML, HTML?
- 💾 **Content Length** - ¿Tamaño respuesta?
